/-!
# The height ideals of a formal group law

Let `F` be a formal group law over a commutative ring `R` and let `p` be a prime. The `n`-th
**height ideal** `I_n(F)` (`FormalGroup.heightIdeal`) is the ideal generated by the coefficients of
the `p`-series `[p]_F(X)` in degrees below `pⁿ`. Equivalently, a ring homomorphism `φ : R →+* S`
kills `I_n(F)` exactly when the `p`-series of the base change of `F` along `φ` vanishes to order
`pⁿ` (`FormalGroup.heightIdeal_le_ker_iff`), so `R ⧸ I_n(F)` is the universal quotient of `R` over
which `[p]_F` vanishes to order `pⁿ`. Over a field of characteristic `p` the height ideal `I_n`
is zero when the height of `F` is at least `n`, and the unit ideal otherwise
(`FormalGroup.heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff_le_height`, `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_eq_top_iff_height_lt`).

For commutative `F` these are Landweber's ideals `I_n = (v₀, v₁, …, v_(n-1))`: `I₀ = 0`, `I₁ = (p)`,
and `I_(n+1) = I_n + (v_n)`, where `v_n` is the coefficient of `X^(pⁿ)` in `[p]_F`
(`FormalGroup.heightIdeal_succ`). Only the class of `v_n` modulo `I_n` up to a unit factor matters
(`FormalGroup.heightIdeal_succ_eq_sup_of_sub_mul_mem`,
`FormalGroup.heightIdeal_succ_eq_sup_of_sub_mem`). The proof works over `R ⧸ (I_n + (v_n))`: there
`p = 0`, so the `p`-series of a commutative formal group law is either zero or has order a power
of `p` (`FormalGroup.exists_order_nsmulSeries_eq_pow`), and order greater than `pⁿ` then forces
order at least `p^(n+1)`. Consequently, any sequence of lifts of `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` modulo
`I₀, …, I_(n-1)` generates `I_n` (`FormalGroup.ofList_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem`), and
whenever the height ideals `I₀ < I₁ < … < I_n` are strictly increasing with `I₀, …, I_(n-1)` prime
and `I_n ≠ ⊤`, any such sequence is a regular sequence on `R`
(`FormalGroup.isRegular_ofFn_of_sub_mem_heightIdeal`).

The height ideals do not depend on the coordinate: isomorphic formal group laws have the same
height ideals (`TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.heightIdeal_eq`), and the height ideals commute with base
change (`FormalGroup.map_heightIdeal`). For the universal formal group law over the Lazard ring `L`
and the universal strict coordinate change over `L[b₁, b₂, …]`, this says that the height ideals of
`L` are invariant ideals of the Hopf algebroid `(L, L[b₁, b₂, …])`: their extensions along the left
and right units agree (`TauCeti.LazardRing.map_rightUnit_heightIdeal`, stated with the rest
of the Hopf algebroid in `TauCeti.RingTheory.FormalGroup.CoordinateChange.HopfAlgebroid`).
Through Quillen's identification of `L` with `MU_*`, these are the ideals `I_(p,n)` in the
hypothesis of Landweber's exact functor theorem.

The class of `v_n` modulo `I_n` transforms by a unit power under coordinate change. Modulo
`I_n(F) + I_n(G)` both `p`-series begin in degree `pⁿ`, so a homomorphism `F → G` with linear
coefficient `u` relates their coefficients `a` and `b` of `X^(pⁿ)` by `b u^(pⁿ) ≡ u a`
(`TauCeti.FormalGroupHom.coeff_nsmulSeries_mul_coeff_one_pow_sub_mem_heightIdeal`), an arbitrary
isomorphism rescales `v_n` modulo `I_n` by `(u⁻¹)^(pⁿ) u`
(`TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.coeff_nsmulSeries_sub_unit_mul_mem_heightIdeal`), and a strict
isomorphism preserves the class of `v_n`
(`TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.coeff_nsmulSeries_sub_mem_heightIdeal_of_isStrict`). Over `L` this is the
congruence `η_R(v_n) ≡ η_L(v_n)` modulo `I_n`
(`TauCeti.LazardRing.rightUnit_sub_C_mem_map_heightIdeal`).

For `n > 0`, the height ideal `I_n` is the unit ideal exactly when every specialization to a
field of characteristic `p` has height less than `n`. Only fields in the universe of the
coefficient ring are needed, since maximal-ideal quotients detect a proper ideal. Thus field
height bounds imply ideal-theoretic bounds without reducedness or Noetherian hypotheses.
Landweber's recursion identifies the unit-ideal condition for `I_(n+1)` with invertibility
of `v_n` modulo `I_n`.

## Main definitions

* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal`: the ideal generated by the coefficients of `[p]_F` below degree `pⁿ`.

## Main results

* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_le_ker_iff`: a ring homomorphism kills `I_n(F)` exactly when the
  `p`-series of the base change of `F` vanishes to order `pⁿ`.
* `FormalGroup.map_heightIdeal`: the height ideals commute with base change.
* `TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.heightIdeal_eq`: isomorphic formal group laws have the same height
  ideals.
* `TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.coeff_nsmulSeries_sub_unit_mul_mem_heightIdeal` and
  `TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.coeff_nsmulSeries_sub_mem_heightIdeal_of_isStrict`: isomorphisms rescale
  `v_n` modulo `I_n` by a unit, and strict isomorphisms preserve it.
* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_𝔾ₘ_eq_top` and `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_𝔾ₐ`: `I_n(𝔾ₘ)` is the unit
  ideal for `n ≥ 2`, while `I_n(𝔾ₐ) = (p)` for `n ≥ 1`.
* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_succ`: `I_(n+1) = I_n + (v_n)` for commutative `F`.
* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_one`: `I₁ = (p)` for commutative `F`.
* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_eq_span`: `I_n = (v₀, …, v_(n-1))` for commutative `F`.
* `FormalGroup.iSup_heightIdeal_le_ker_iff` and `FormalGroup.iSup_heightIdeal_eq_span`: for
  `1 < p`, a ring homomorphism kills `⨆ n, I_n(F)` exactly when the `p`-series vanishes, and for
  commutative `F` and prime `p`, `⨆ n, I_n(F) = (v₀, v₁, v₂, …)`.
* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff_le_height`: over a field of characteristic `p`, `I_n = 0`
  exactly when `F` has height at least `n`.
* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_le_ker_iff_le_height`,
  `FormalGroup.iSup_heightIdeal_le_ker_iff_height_eq_top`,
  `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_le_prime_iff`, and `FormalGroup.iSup_heightIdeal_le_prime_iff`: a
  homomorphism into a field kills `I_n(F)` (for commutative `F` and prime `p`) iff the base-changed
  law has `p`-height at least `n` and kills `⨆ n, I_n(F)` (for `1 < p`) iff that law has infinite
  `p`-height; in particular this characterizes the prime ideals `P` containing `I_n(F)` and
  `⨆ n, I_n(F)` through `P.ResidueField`.
* `FormalGroup.heightIdeal_eq_top_iff_forall_height_lt`: positive-index height ideals are the
  unit ideal exactly when all characteristic-`p` field specializations have height below the index.
* `FormalGroup.isUnit_mk_coeff_nsmulSeries_iff`: `v_n` is a unit modulo `I_n` exactly when
  `I_(n+1)` is the unit ideal.

## References

* P. S. Landweber, *Homological properties of comodules over `MU_*(MU)` and `BP_*(BP)`*,
  Amer. J. Math. 98 (1976), 591–610.
* D. C. Ravenel, *Complex Cobordism and Stable Homotopy Groups of Spheres*, Chapter 4.
-/

public section

namespace FormalGroup

variable {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]

/-- The `n`-th **height ideal** of a formal group law `F` at `p`: the ideal generated by the
coefficients of the `p`-series `[p]_F(X)` in degrees below `pⁿ`, that is, the smallest ideal
modulo which `[p]_F` vanishes to order `pⁿ`. -/
noncomputable def heightIdeal (F : FormalGroup R) (p n : ℕ) : Ideal R :=
  Ideal.span ((fun k ↦ PowerSeries.coeff k (F.nsmulSeries p)) '' Set.Iio (p ^ n))

theorem heightIdeal_def (F : FormalGroup R) (p n : ℕ) :
    F.heightIdeal p n =
      Ideal.span ((fun k ↦ PowerSeries.coeff k (F.nsmulSeries p)) '' Set.Iio (p ^ n)) :=
  (rfl)

variable {F : FormalGroup R} {p : ℕ}

/-- The height ideal `I_n(F)` is contained in an ideal `I` exactly when the coefficients of `[p]_F`
below degree `pⁿ` lie in `I`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_le_iff {n : ℕ} {I : Ideal R} :
    F.heightIdeal p n ≤ I ↔ ∀ k < p ^ n, PowerSeries.coeff k (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ I := by
  simp [heightIdeal, Ideal.span_le, Set.subset_def]

/-- The coefficients of `[p]_F` below degree `pⁿ` lie in the height ideal `I_n(F)`. -/
theorem coeff_nsmulSeries_mem_heightIdeal {n k : ℕ} (hk : k < p ^ n) :
    PowerSeries.coeff k (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p n :=
  heightIdeal_le_iff.mp le_rfl k hk

/-- **The universal property of the height ideal.** A ring homomorphism `φ` kills `I_n(F)` exactly
when the `p`-series of the base change of `F` along `φ` vanishes to order `pⁿ`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_le_ker_iff {n : ℕ} (φ : R →+* S) :
    F.heightIdeal p n ≤ RingHom.ker φ ↔ ((p ^ n : ℕ) : ℕ∞) ≤ ((F.map φ).nsmulSeries p).order := by
  simp only [heightIdeal_le_iff, RingHom.mem_ker, PowerSeries.nat_le_order_iff,
    coeff_nsmulSeries_map]

/-- The height ideal `I_n(F)` vanishes exactly when `[p]_F` vanishes to order `pⁿ`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff {n : ℕ} :
    F.heightIdeal p n = ⊥ ↔ ((p ^ n : ℕ) : ℕ∞) ≤ (F.nsmulSeries p).order := by
  simp only [← le_bot_iff, heightIdeal_le_iff, Ideal.mem_bot, PowerSeries.nat_le_order_iff]

/-- The zeroth height ideal is zero, since `[p]_F` has no constant term. -/
@[simp]
theorem heightIdeal_zero : F.heightIdeal p 0 = ⊥ := by
  rw [heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff, pow_zero, Nat.cast_one, Order.one_le_iff_ne_zero,
    PowerSeries.order_ne_zero_iff_constCoeff_eq_zero]
  exact F.constantCoeff_nsmulSeries p

/-- The height ideals increase with `n`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_mono : Monotone (F.heightIdeal p) := fun _ _ hmn ↦
  heightIdeal_le_iff.mpr fun _ hk ↦ by
    rcases p.eq_zero_or_pos with rfl | hp
    · simp
    · exact coeff_nsmulSeries_mem_heightIdeal (hk.trans_le (Nat.pow_le_pow_right hp hmn))

/-- The height ideals commute with base change. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_heightIdeal (φ : R →+* S) (n : ℕ) :
    (F.heightIdeal p n).map φ = (F.map φ).heightIdeal p n := by
  simp only [heightIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_image, coeff_nsmulSeries_map]

/-- The supremum of the height ideals commutes with base change. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_iSup_heightIdeal (φ : R →+* S) :
    (⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n).map φ = ⨆ n, (F.map φ).heightIdeal p n := by
  simp [Ideal.map_iSup]

/-- For `1 < p`, the supremum `⨆ n, I_n(F)` of the height ideals is contained in an ideal `I`
exactly when all coefficients of `[p]_F` lie in `I`. -/
theorem iSup_heightIdeal_le_iff (hp : 1 < p) {I : Ideal R} :
    ⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n ≤ I ↔ ∀ k, PowerSeries.coeff k (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ I := by
  simp only [iSup_le_iff, heightIdeal_le_iff]
  exact ⟨fun h k ↦ h k k (k.lt_pow_self hp), fun h _ k _ ↦ h k⟩

/-- For `1 < p`, every coefficient of `[p]_F` lies in `⨆ n, I_n(F)`. -/
theorem coeff_nsmulSeries_mem_iSup_heightIdeal (hp : 1 < p) (k : ℕ) :
    PowerSeries.coeff k (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ ⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n :=
  (iSup_heightIdeal_le_iff hp).mp le_rfl k

/-- **The universal property of the infinite height ideal.** For `1 < p`, a ring homomorphism `φ`
kills `⨆ n, I_n(F)` exactly when the `p`-series of the base change of `F` along `φ` vanishes. -/
theorem iSup_heightIdeal_le_ker_iff (hp : 1 < p) (φ : R →+* S) :
    ⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n ≤ RingHom.ker φ ↔ (F.map φ).nsmulSeries p = 0 := by
  rw [iSup_heightIdeal_le_iff hp, PowerSeries.ext_iff]
  simp [RingHom.mem_ker, coeff_nsmulSeries_map]

/-- For `1 < p`, the supremum `⨆ n, I_n(F)` vanishes exactly when `[p]_F = 0`. -/
theorem iSup_heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff (hp : 1 < p) :
    ⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n = ⊥ ↔ F.nsmulSeries p = 0 := by
  rw [← le_bot_iff, iSup_heightIdeal_le_iff hp, PowerSeries.ext_iff]
  simp

end FormalGroup

/-- **Coordinate independence of the height ideals**: isomorphic formal group laws have the same
height ideals. -/
theorem TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.heightIdeal_eq {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {F G : FormalGroup R}
    (e : FormalGroupIso F G) (p n : ℕ) : F.heightIdeal p n = G.heightIdeal p n := by
  suffices h : ∀ {F G : FormalGroup R}, FormalGroupIso F G → F.heightIdeal p n ≤ G.heightIdeal p n
    from le_antisymm (h e) (h e.symm)
  intro F G e
  rw [← Ideal.mk_ker (I := G.heightIdeal p n), FormalGroup.heightIdeal_le_ker_iff,
    (e.map _).order_nsmulSeries_eq, ← FormalGroup.heightIdeal_le_ker_iff, Ideal.mk_ker]

/-- **A homomorphism relates the coefficients `v_n` modulo the height ideals.** If `f` is a
homomorphism of formal group laws from `F` to `G` with linear coefficient `u`, and `a` and `b` are
the coefficients of `X^(pⁿ)` in `[p]_F` and `[p]_G`, then `b u^(pⁿ) ≡ u a` modulo
`I_n(F) + I_n(G)`. -/
theorem TauCeti.FormalGroupHom.coeff_nsmulSeries_mul_coeff_one_pow_sub_mem_heightIdeal
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {F G : FormalGroup R} (f : FormalGroupHom F G) (p n : ℕ) :
    PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (G.nsmulSeries p) * PowerSeries.coeff 1 f.toPowerSeries ^ (p ^ n) -
        PowerSeries.coeff 1 f.toPowerSeries * PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈
      F.heightIdeal p n ⊔ G.heightIdeal p n := by
  set I := F.heightIdeal p n ⊔ G.heightIdeal p n
  -- modulo `I`, both `p`-series vanish to order `pⁿ`
  have hle (H : FormalGroup R) (hH : H.heightIdeal p n ≤ I) :
      ((p ^ n : ℕ) : ℕ∞) ≤ ((H.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).nsmulSeries p).order := by
    rwa [← FormalGroup.heightIdeal_le_ker_iff, Ideal.mk_ker]
  rw [← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, map_sub, sub_eq_zero]
  simpa [FormalGroup.coeff_nsmulSeries_map] using
    (f.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk I)).coeff_nsmulSeries_mul_coeff_one_pow_of_le_order p
      (hle F le_sup_left) (hle G le_sup_right)

/-- **Coordinate scaling of `v_n` modulo `I_n`.** Under an arbitrary isomorphism `e` of formal group
laws from `F` to `G` with linear coefficient unit `u`, the coefficient of `X^(pⁿ)` in `[p]_G` agrees
with `(u⁻¹)^(pⁿ) u` times that of `[p]_F` modulo `I_n(F) = I_n(G)`. -/
theorem TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.coeff_nsmulSeries_sub_unit_mul_mem_heightIdeal
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {F G : FormalGroup R} (e : FormalGroupIso F G) (p n : ℕ) :
    PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (G.nsmulSeries p) -
        ↑(e.isUnit_coeff_one.unit⁻¹ ^ p ^ n * e.isUnit_coeff_one.unit) *
          PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈
      F.heightIdeal p n := by
  set u : Rˣ := e.isUnit_coeff_one.unit
  have hu : (u : R) = PowerSeries.coeff 1 e.toHom.toPowerSeries := IsUnit.unit_spec _
  have h := e.toHom.coeff_nsmulSeries_mul_coeff_one_pow_sub_mem_heightIdeal p n
  rw [← hu, ← e.heightIdeal_eq, sup_idem] at h
  convert Ideal.mul_mem_left _ ((u⁻¹ : Rˣ) ^ p ^ n : R) h using 1
  rw [Units.val_mul, Units.val_pow_eq_pow_val, mul_sub, ← mul_assoc,
    mul_right_comm _ _ ((u : R) ^ _), ← mul_pow, Units.inv_mul, one_pow, one_mul, mul_assoc]

/-- **Coordinate independence of `v_n` modulo `I_n`.** If `e` is a strict isomorphism of formal
group laws from `F` to `G`, then the coefficients of `X^(pⁿ)` in `[p]_F` and `[p]_G` agree modulo
the height ideal `I_n(F) = I_n(G)`. -/
theorem TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.coeff_nsmulSeries_sub_mem_heightIdeal_of_isStrict
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {F G : FormalGroup R} (e : FormalGroupIso F G) [e.IsStrict]
    (p n : ℕ) :
    PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (G.nsmulSeries p) - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈
      F.heightIdeal p n := by
  have h := e.toHom.coeff_nsmulSeries_mul_coeff_one_pow_sub_mem_heightIdeal p n
  rwa [FormalGroupIso.IsStrict.coeff_one, one_pow, mul_one, one_mul, ← e.heightIdeal_eq,
    sup_idem] at h

namespace FormalGroup

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {p : ℕ}

/-- The height ideals are unchanged by a change of coordinate `φ • F`. -/
@[simp]
theorem heightIdeal_smul (φ : TauCeti.FormalCoordinate R) (F : FormalGroup R) (n : ℕ) :
    (φ • F).heightIdeal p n = F.heightIdeal p n :=
  ((smulIso φ F).heightIdeal_eq p n).symm

/-- The height ideals of the multiplicative formal group law `X + Y + XY` from `I₂` on are the unit
ideal: the coefficient of `Xᵖ` in its `p`-series `(1 + X)ᵖ - 1` is `1`. -/
@[simp]
theorem heightIdeal_𝔾ₘ_eq_top (hp : 1 < p) {n : ℕ} (hn : 2 ≤ n) :
    (𝔾ₘ : FormalGroup R).heightIdeal p n = ⊤ := by
  have hn' : 1 < n := by omega
  rw [Ideal.eq_top_iff_one]
  convert coeff_nsmulSeries_mem_heightIdeal (F := (𝔾ₘ : FormalGroup R)) (k := p)
    (by simpa using Nat.pow_lt_pow_right hp hn')
  rw [nsmulSeries_𝔾ₘ, map_sub, add_comm, add_pow]
  simp [PowerSeries.coeff_X_pow, PowerSeries.coeff_one, (zero_lt_one.trans hp).ne']

/-- The height ideals `I_n` of the additive formal group law `X + Y` with `n ≥ 1` are all `(p)`:
its `p`-series `p X` has no coefficient beyond the linear one. -/
@[simp]
theorem heightIdeal_𝔾ₐ (hp : 1 < p) {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≠ 0) :
    (𝔾ₐ : FormalGroup R).heightIdeal p n = Ideal.span {(p : R)} := by
  refine le_antisymm (heightIdeal_le_iff.mpr fun k _ ↦ ?_) ?_
  · rw [nsmulSeries_𝔾ₐ, PowerSeries.coeff_natCast_mul, PowerSeries.coeff_X]
    split_ifs <;> simp
  · rw [Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem]
    convert coeff_nsmulSeries_mem_heightIdeal (F := (𝔾ₐ : FormalGroup R)) (k := 1)
      (Nat.one_lt_pow hn hp) using 1
    simp

variable (F : FormalGroup R) [F.IsComm]

/-- **Landweber's recursion for the height ideals.** For a commutative formal group law `F` and a
prime `p`, `I_(n+1)(F) = I_n(F) + (v_n)`, where `v_n` is the coefficient of `X^(pⁿ)` in `[p]_F`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_succ (hp : p.Prime) (n : ℕ) :
    F.heightIdeal p (n + 1) =
      F.heightIdeal p n ⊔ Ideal.span {PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p)} := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (sup_le (heightIdeal_mono n.le_succ)
    ((Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem _).mpr
      (coeff_nsmulSeries_mem_heightIdeal (Nat.pow_lt_pow_right hp.one_lt n.lt_succ_self))))
  set J := F.heightIdeal p n ⊔ Ideal.span {PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p)}
  have hJ (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ p ^ n) : PowerSeries.coeff k (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ J := by
    rcases hk.lt_or_eq with hk | rfl
    · exact Ideal.mem_sup_left (coeff_nsmulSeries_mem_heightIdeal hk)
    · exact Ideal.mem_sup_right (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)
  rw [← Ideal.mk_ker (I := J), heightIdeal_le_ker_iff]
  -- over `R ⧸ J`, the prime `p` vanishes, since it is the linear coefficient of `[p]_F`
  have hpJ : ((p : ℕ) : R ⧸ J) = 0 := by
    rw [← map_natCast (Ideal.Quotient.mk J), ← F.coeff_one_nsmulSeries p,
      Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact hJ 1 (Nat.one_le_pow _ _ hp.pos)
  -- and the `p`-series vanishes to order `pⁿ + 1`
  have hord : ((p ^ n + 1 : ℕ) : ℕ∞) ≤ ((F.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)).nsmulSeries p).order := by
    refine PowerSeries.nat_le_order _ _ fun k hk ↦ ?_
    rw [coeff_nsmulSeries_map, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact hJ k (Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp hk)
  -- so its order, a power `p ^ h` of `p`, has `h > n`
  by_cases h0 : (F.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)).nsmulSeries p = 0
  · simp [h0]
  obtain ⟨h, -, hh⟩ := (F.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)).exists_order_nsmulSeries_eq_pow hp hpJ h0
  rw [hh, Nat.cast_le] at hord ⊢
  exact Nat.pow_le_pow_right hp.pos ((Nat.pow_lt_pow_iff_right hp.one_lt).mp hord)

/-- Landweber's element `v_n` is a unit modulo `I_n` exactly when the next height
ideal is the unit ideal. This also applies when the quotient is the zero ring. -/
theorem isUnit_mk_coeff_nsmulSeries_iff (hp : p.Prime) (n : ℕ) :
    IsUnit (Ideal.Quotient.mk (F.heightIdeal p n)
      (PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p))) ↔ F.heightIdeal p (n + 1) = ⊤ := by
  rw [Ideal.Quotient.isUnit_mk_iff, F.heightIdeal_succ hp, sup_comm]

/-- The recursion `I_(n+1) = I_n + (v_n)` holds for every lift `v` of a unit multiple `c * v_n`
modulo `I_n`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_succ_eq_sup_of_sub_mul_mem (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ} {c v : R} (hc : IsUnit c)
    (hv : v - c * PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p n) :
    F.heightIdeal p (n + 1) = F.heightIdeal p n ⊔ Ideal.span {v} := by
  rw [F.heightIdeal_succ hp, ← Ideal.span_singleton_mul_left_unit hc]
  refine le_antisymm (sup_le le_sup_left ?_) (sup_le le_sup_left ?_) <;>
    rw [Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem]
  · exact sub_sub_cancel v (c * PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p)) ▸
      Ideal.sub_mem _ (Ideal.mem_sup_right (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self v))
        (Ideal.mem_sup_left hv)
  · exact sub_add_cancel v (c * PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p)) ▸
      Ideal.add_mem _ (Ideal.mem_sup_left hv)
        (Ideal.mem_sup_right (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _))

/-- The recursion `I_(n+1) = I_n + (v_n)` holds for every lift `v` of `v_n` modulo `I_n`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_succ_eq_sup_of_sub_mem (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ} {v : R}
    (hv : v - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p n) :
    F.heightIdeal p (n + 1) = F.heightIdeal p n ⊔ Ideal.span {v} :=
  F.heightIdeal_succ_eq_sup_of_sub_mul_mem hp isUnit_one (by simpa using hv)

/-- The first height ideal is generated by `p`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_one (hp : p.Prime) : F.heightIdeal p 1 = Ideal.span {(p : R)} := by
  simpa using F.heightIdeal_succ hp 0

/-- **Landweber's generators.** `I_n(F) = (v₀, …, v_(n-1))`, where `v_i` is the coefficient of
`X^(pⁱ)` in `[p]_F`; in particular `v₀ = p`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_eq_span (hp : p.Prime) (n : ℕ) :
    F.heightIdeal p n =
      Ideal.span ((fun i ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ i) (F.nsmulSeries p)) '' Set.Iio n) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simp
  | succ n ih =>
    have hI : Set.Iio (n + 1) = insert n (Set.Iio n) := by
      ext; simp
    rw [F.heightIdeal_succ hp, ih, hI, Set.image_insert_eq, Ideal.span_insert, sup_comm]

/-- **Landweber's generators for the infinite height ideal.** For a commutative formal group law
`F` and a prime `p`, `⨆ n, I_n(F) = (v₀, v₁, v₂, …)`, where `v_i` is the coefficient of `X^(pⁱ)` in
`[p]_F`. -/
theorem iSup_heightIdeal_eq_span (hp : p.Prime) :
    ⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ i) (F.nsmulSeries p)) := by
  have hIio : ⋃ n : ℕ, Set.Iio n = Set.univ :=
    Set.ext fun i ↦ ⟨fun _ ↦ trivial, fun _ ↦ Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨i + 1, i.lt_succ_self⟩⟩
  simp_rw [F.heightIdeal_eq_span hp, ← Ideal.span_iUnion, ← Set.image_iUnion, hIio, Set.image_univ]

/-- For a sequence `v` of unit-scaled lifts of `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` modulo `I₀, …, I_(n-1)`, the first
`k` entries generate `I_k(F)`. -/
theorem ofList_take_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mul_mem (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ} {c v : Fin n → R}
    (hc : ∀ i, IsUnit (c i))
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - c i * PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i)
    {k : ℕ} (hk : k ≤ n) :
    Ideal.ofList ((List.ofFn v).take k) = F.heightIdeal p k := by
  induction k with
  | zero => simp
  | succ k ih =>
    have htake :
        (List.ofFn v).take (k + 1) = (List.ofFn v).take k ++ [v ⟨k, Nat.lt_of_succ_le hk⟩] := by
      simp [List.take_add_one, Nat.lt_of_succ_le hk]
    rw [htake, Ideal.ofList_append, Ideal.ofList_singleton, ih (Nat.le_of_succ_le hk),
      F.heightIdeal_succ_eq_sup_of_sub_mul_mem hp (hc _) (hv ⟨k, Nat.lt_of_succ_le hk⟩)]

/-- For a sequence `v` of lifts of `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` modulo `I₀, …, I_(n-1)`, the first `k` entries
generate `I_k(F)`. -/
theorem ofList_take_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ} {v : Fin n → R}
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i)
    {k : ℕ} (hk : k ≤ n) :
    Ideal.ofList ((List.ofFn v).take k) = F.heightIdeal p k :=
  F.ofList_take_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mul_mem hp (c := fun _ ↦ 1) (fun _ ↦ isUnit_one)
    (by simpa using hv) hk

/-- Any sequence `v` of unit-scaled lifts of `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` modulo `I₀, …, I_(n-1)` generates
`I_n(F)`. -/
theorem ofList_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mul_mem (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ} {c v : Fin n → R}
    (hc : ∀ i, IsUnit (c i))
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - c i * PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i) :
    Ideal.ofList (List.ofFn v) = F.heightIdeal p n := by
  simpa [List.take_of_length_le] using
    F.ofList_take_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mul_mem hp hc hv le_rfl

/-- Any sequence `v` of lifts of `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` modulo `I₀, …, I_(n-1)` generates `I_n(F)`. -/
theorem ofList_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ} {v : Fin n → R}
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i) :
    Ideal.ofList (List.ofFn v) = F.heightIdeal p n :=
  F.ofList_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mul_mem hp (c := fun _ ↦ 1) (fun _ ↦ isUnit_one)
    (by simpa using hv)

/-- The list `[v₀, …, v_(n-1)]` of `p`-series coefficients generates `I_n(F)`. -/
theorem ofList_ofFn_coeff_nsmulSeries_eq_heightIdeal (hp : p.Prime) (n : ℕ) :
    Ideal.ofList (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p)) =
      F.heightIdeal p n :=
  F.ofList_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem hp fun i ↦ by simp

/-- If `I_n(F) < I_(n+1)(F)`, no lift `v` of `v_n` modulo `I_n(F)` lies in `I_n(F)`. -/
theorem notMem_heightIdeal_of_lt_succ_of_sub_mem (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ}
    (hlt : F.heightIdeal p n < F.heightIdeal p (n + 1)) {v : R}
    (hv : v - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p n) :
    v ∉ F.heightIdeal p n := by
  intro hv_mem
  refine hlt.ne.symm ?_
  rw [F.heightIdeal_succ_eq_sup_of_sub_mem hp hv, sup_eq_left, Ideal.span_singleton_le_iff_mem]
  exact hv_mem

/-- If `I_n(F)` is prime and strictly smaller than `I_(n+1)(F)`, every lift `v` of `v_n` modulo
`I_n(F)` acts regularly on `R ⧸ I_n(F)`. -/
theorem isSMulRegular_quotient_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ}
    (hprime : (F.heightIdeal p n).IsPrime)
    (hlt : F.heightIdeal p n < F.heightIdeal p (n + 1)) {v : R}
    (hv : v - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ n) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p n) :
    IsSMulRegular (R ⧸ F.heightIdeal p n) v := by
  rw [isSMulRegular_quotient_iff_mem_of_smul_mem]
  intro x hvx
  rw [smul_eq_mul] at hvx
  exact (hprime.mul_mem_iff_mem_or_mem.mp hvx).resolve_left
    (F.notMem_heightIdeal_of_lt_succ_of_sub_mem hp hlt hv)

/-- **Weak regularity from a chain of prime height ideals.** If `I₀(F) < I₁(F) < … < I_n(F)` and
`I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` are prime, then any sequence of lifts of `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` modulo
`I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` is weakly regular on `R`. -/
theorem isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_of_sub_mem_heightIdeal (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ}
    (hprime : ∀ i < n, (F.heightIdeal p i).IsPrime)
    (hlt : ∀ i < n, F.heightIdeal p i < F.heightIdeal p (i + 1)) {v : Fin n → R}
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular R (List.ofFn v) := by
  refine ⟨fun i hi ↦ ?_⟩
  have hi' : i < n := by simpa using hi
  rw [F.ofList_take_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem hp hv hi'.le, Ideal.smul_eq_mul,
    Ideal.mul_top, List.getElem_ofFn]
  exact F.isSMulRegular_quotient_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem hp (hprime i hi') (hlt i hi') (hv ⟨i, hi'⟩)

/-- **Regularity from a chain of prime height ideals.** If `I₀(F) < I₁(F) < … < I_n(F)` with
`I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` prime and `I_n(F) ≠ ⊤`, then any sequence of lifts of `v₀, …, v_(n-1)`
modulo `I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` is a regular sequence on `R`. -/
theorem isRegular_ofFn_of_sub_mem_heightIdeal (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ}
    (hprime : ∀ i < n, (F.heightIdeal p i).IsPrime)
    (hlt : ∀ i < n, F.heightIdeal p i < F.heightIdeal p (i + 1))
    (hne : F.heightIdeal p n ≠ ⊤) {v : Fin n → R}
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R (List.ofFn v) :=
  ⟨F.isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_of_sub_mem_heightIdeal hp hprime hlt hv, by
    rw [F.ofList_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem hp hv, Ideal.smul_eq_mul, Ideal.mul_top]
    exact hne.symm⟩

/-- If `I₀(F) < I₁(F) < … < I_n(F)` with `I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` prime and `I_n(F) ≠ ⊤`, then the
`p`-series coefficients `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` form a regular sequence on `R`. -/
theorem isRegular_ofFn_coeff_nsmulSeries (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ}
    (hprime : ∀ i < n, (F.heightIdeal p i).IsPrime)
    (hlt : ∀ i < n, F.heightIdeal p i < F.heightIdeal p (i + 1))
    (hne : F.heightIdeal p n ≠ ⊤) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R
      (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p)) :=
  F.isRegular_ofFn_of_sub_mem_heightIdeal hp hprime hlt hne fun _ ↦ by simp

/-- **Unit-scaled lift invariance of weak regularity on modules.** For any `R`-module `M`, a
sequence `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` congruent to unit multiples of `[X] [p]_F(X), …, [X^(p^(n-1))] [p]_F(X)`
modulo `I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` is weakly regular on `M` if and only if the `p`-series coefficients
themselves are weakly regular on `M`. -/
theorem isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mul_mem_heightIdeal (hp : p.Prime) (M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {n : ℕ} {c v : Fin n → R} (hc : ∀ i, IsUnit (c i))
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - c i * PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular M (List.ofFn v) ↔
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular M
        (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p)) := by
  rw [RingTheory.Sequence.isWeaklyRegular_iff, RingTheory.Sequence.isWeaklyRegular_iff]
  simp only [List.length_ofFn, List.getElem_ofFn]
  refine forall₂_congr fun i hi ↦ ?_
  rw [F.ofList_take_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mul_mem hp hc hv hi.le,
    F.ofList_take_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mem hp (fun _ ↦ by simp) hi.le,
    Ideal.isSMulRegular_quotient_smul_top_congr _ (hv ⟨i, hi⟩), IsSMulRegular.mul_iff]
  exact and_iff_right ((hc ⟨i, hi⟩).isSMulRegular _)

/-- **Lift invariance of weak regularity on modules.** For any `R`-module `M`, a sequence of lifts
`v₀, …, v_(n-1)` modulo `I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` is weakly regular on `M` if and only if the
`p`-series coefficients `[X] [p]_F(X), …, [X^(p^(n-1))] [p]_F(X)` are weakly regular on `M`. -/
theorem isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mem_heightIdeal (hp : p.Prime) (M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {n : ℕ} {v : Fin n → R}
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular M (List.ofFn v) ↔
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular M
        (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p)) :=
  F.isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mul_mem_heightIdeal hp M (c := fun _ ↦ 1)
    (fun _ ↦ isUnit_one) (by simpa using hv)

/-- **Unit-scaled lift invariance of regularity on modules.** For any `R`-module `M`, a sequence
`v₀, …, v_(n-1)` congruent to unit multiples of `[X] [p]_F(X), …, [X^(p^(n-1))] [p]_F(X)` modulo
`I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` is regular on `M` if and only if the `p`-series coefficients themselves are
regular on `M`. -/
theorem isRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mul_mem_heightIdeal (hp : p.Prime) (M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {n : ℕ} {c v : Fin n → R} (hc : ∀ i, IsUnit (c i))
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - c i * PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M (List.ofFn v) ↔
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M
        (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p)) := by
  rw [RingTheory.Sequence.isRegular_iff, RingTheory.Sequence.isRegular_iff,
    F.isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mul_mem_heightIdeal hp M hc hv,
    F.ofList_ofFn_eq_heightIdeal_of_sub_mul_mem hp hc hv,
    F.ofList_ofFn_coeff_nsmulSeries_eq_heightIdeal hp n]

/-- **Lift invariance of regularity on modules.** For any `R`-module `M`, a sequence of lifts
`v₀, …, v_(n-1)` modulo `I₀(F), …, I_(n-1)(F)` is regular on `M` if and only if the `p`-series
coefficients `[X] [p]_F(X), …, [X^(p^(n-1))] [p]_F(X)` are regular on `M`. -/
theorem isRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mem_heightIdeal (hp : p.Prime) (M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] {n : ℕ} {v : Fin n → R}
    (hv : ∀ i : Fin n,
      v i - PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p) ∈ F.heightIdeal p i) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M (List.ofFn v) ↔
      RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M
        (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p)) :=
  F.isRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mul_mem_heightIdeal hp M (c := fun _ ↦ 1)
    (fun _ ↦ isUnit_one) (by simpa using hv)

omit [F.IsComm] in
/-- The height ideals of a formal group law are finitely generated. -/
theorem heightIdeal_fg (n : ℕ) : (F.heightIdeal p n).FG :=
  Submodule.fg_span ((Set.finite_Iio (p ^ n)).image _)

end FormalGroup

/-- **Coordinate invariance of Landweber weak regularity on modules.** Any isomorphism from a
commutative formal group law `F` to `G` (not necessarily strict) preserves weak regularity of the
`p`-series coefficients `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` on any `R`-module `M`. -/
theorem TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_coeff_nsmulSeries_iff
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {F G : FormalGroup R} [F.IsComm]
    (e : FormalGroupIso F G) {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (n : ℕ) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular M
      (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (G.nsmulSeries p)) ↔
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsWeaklyRegular M
      (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p)) :=
  F.isWeaklyRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mul_mem_heightIdeal hp M (fun _ ↦ Units.isUnit _) fun i ↦
    e.coeff_nsmulSeries_sub_unit_mul_mem_heightIdeal p i

/-- **Coordinate invariance of Landweber regularity on modules.** Any isomorphism from a
commutative formal group law `F` to `G` (not necessarily strict) preserves regularity of the
`p`-series coefficients `v₀, …, v_(n-1)` on any `R`-module `M`. -/
theorem TauCeti.FormalGroupIso.isRegular_ofFn_coeff_nsmulSeries_iff
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {F G : FormalGroup R} [F.IsComm]
    (e : FormalGroupIso F G) {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (M : Type*)
    [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] (n : ℕ) :
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M
      (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (G.nsmulSeries p)) ↔
    RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular M
      (List.ofFn fun i : Fin n ↦ PowerSeries.coeff (p ^ (i : ℕ)) (F.nsmulSeries p)) :=
  F.isRegular_ofFn_iff_of_sub_mul_mem_heightIdeal hp M (fun _ ↦ Units.isUnit _) fun i ↦
    e.coeff_nsmulSeries_sub_unit_mul_mem_heightIdeal p i

namespace FormalGroup

variable {K : Type*} [Field K] (F : FormalGroup K) [F.IsComm] {p : ℕ} [CharP K p]

/-- Over a field of characteristic `p`, the height ideal `I_n(F)` is zero exactly when `F` has
height at least `n`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff_le_height {n : ℕ} : F.heightIdeal p n = ⊥ ↔ n ≤ F.height p := by
  rw [heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff]
  by_cases h0 : F.nsmulSeries p = 0
  · simp [h0, F.height_eq_top_iff.mpr h0]
  obtain hp | rfl := CharP.char_is_prime_or_zero K p
  · obtain ⟨h, -, hh⟩ := F.exists_order_nsmulSeries_eq_pow hp (CharP.cast_eq_zero K p) h0
    rw [hh, F.height_eq_natCast_iff.mpr hh, Nat.cast_le, Nat.cast_le,
      Nat.pow_le_pow_iff_right hp.one_lt]
  · exact absurd (by simp) h0

/-- Over a field of characteristic `p`, the height ideal `I_n(F)` is the unit ideal exactly when `F`
has height less than `n`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_eq_top_iff_height_lt {n : ℕ} : F.heightIdeal p n = ⊤ ↔ F.height p < n := by
  rw [← not_le, ← heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff_le_height]
  exact ⟨fun h hb ↦ bot_ne_top (hb.symm.trans h), (Ideal.eq_bot_or_top _).resolve_left⟩

omit [F.IsComm] [CharP K p] in
/-- For `1 < p`, the supremum `⨆ n, I_n(F)` vanishes over a field `K` exactly when `F` has infinite
height at `p`. -/
theorem iSup_heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff_height_eq_top (hp : 1 < p) :
    ⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n = ⊥ ↔ F.height p = ⊤ := by
  rw [iSup_heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff hp, F.height_eq_top_iff]

end FormalGroup

namespace FormalGroup

universe u

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (F : FormalGroup R) {p : ℕ}

/-- For `1 < p`, a homomorphism `φ : R →+* K` into a field kills `⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n` if and
only if the base change `F.map φ` has infinite `p`-height. -/
theorem iSup_heightIdeal_le_ker_iff_height_eq_top {K : Type*} [Field K] (hp : 1 < p)
    (φ : R →+* K) :
    ⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n ≤ RingHom.ker φ ↔ (F.map φ).height p = ⊤ := by
  rw [iSup_heightIdeal_le_ker_iff hp, height_eq_top_iff]

/-- **Prime ideals containing `⨆ n, I_n(F)`.** For `1 < p`, a prime ideal `P` of `R` contains the
supremum `⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n` if and only if the specialization of `F` to `P.ResidueField` has
infinite `p`-height. -/
theorem iSup_heightIdeal_le_prime_iff (hp : 1 < p) {P : Ideal R} [P.IsPrime] :
    ⨆ n, F.heightIdeal p n ≤ P ↔
      (F.map (algebraMap R P.ResidueField)).height p = ⊤ := by
  nth_rw 1 [← P.ker_algebraMap_residueField]
  exact F.iSup_heightIdeal_le_ker_iff_height_eq_top hp _

variable [F.IsComm]

/-- A positive-index height ideal is the unit ideal exactly when all characteristic-`p` field
specializations have height below its index. The coefficient ring need not be reduced. -/
theorem heightIdeal_eq_top_iff_forall_height_lt (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ} (hn : n ≠ 0) :
    F.heightIdeal p n = ⊤ ↔
      ∀ (K : Type u) [Field K] [CharP K p] (f : R →+* K), (F.map f).height p < n := by
  constructor
  · intro h K _ _ f
    rw [← heightIdeal_eq_top_iff_height_lt, ← map_heightIdeal, h, Ideal.map_top]
  · intro h
    by_contra hI
    obtain ⟨m, hm, hle⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal (F.heightIdeal p n) hI
    let : m.IsMaximal := hm
    let := Ideal.Quotient.field m
    have hp_mem : (p : R) ∈ m := by
      apply hle
      rw [← F.coeff_one_nsmulSeries p]
      exact coeff_nsmulSeries_mem_heightIdeal (Nat.one_lt_pow hn hp.one_lt)
    let : CharP (R ⧸ m) p := (CharP.charP_iff_prime_eq_zero hp).mpr (by
      rw [← map_natCast (Ideal.Quotient.mk m), Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
      exact hp_mem)
    have htop := (heightIdeal_eq_top_iff_height_lt _).mpr (h (R ⧸ m) (Ideal.Quotient.mk m))
    have hbot : (F.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk m)).heightIdeal p n = ⊥ := by
      rw [← map_heightIdeal]
      exact Ideal.map_mk_eq_bot_of_le hle
    exact bot_ne_top (hbot.symm.trans htop)

/-- For a commutative formal group law `F`, a prime `p`, and any `n : ℕ`, a homomorphism
`φ : R →+* K` into a field kills `F.heightIdeal p n` if and only if the base change `F.map φ` has
`p`-height at least `n`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_le_ker_iff_le_height {K : Type*} [Field K] (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ}
    (φ : R →+* K) :
    F.heightIdeal p n ≤ RingHom.ker φ ↔ (n : ℕ∞) ≤ (F.map φ).height p := by
  rcases eq_or_ne n 0 with rfl | hn
  · simp
  by_cases hpK : (p : K) = 0
  · have : CharP K p := (CharP.charP_iff_prime_eq_zero hp).mpr hpK
    rw [heightIdeal_le_ker_iff, ← heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff, heightIdeal_eq_bot_iff_le_height]
  · have hpφ : (p : R) ∉ RingHom.ker φ := by rwa [RingHom.mem_ker, map_natCast]
    have hnot : ¬ F.heightIdeal p n ≤ RingHom.ker φ := fun hle ↦ hpφ <|
      hle <| F.heightIdeal_mono (Nat.one_le_iff_ne_zero.mpr hn) <| by
        rw [F.heightIdeal_one hp]
        exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
    rw [(F.map φ).height_eq_zero_of_natCast_ne_zero hpK]
    exact iff_of_false hnot (by simpa using hn)

/-- **Prime ideals containing `I_n(F)`.** For a commutative formal group law `F` over `R`, a prime
`p`, any `n : ℕ`, and a prime ideal `P` of `R`, `P` contains `F.heightIdeal p n` if and only if the
specialization of `F` to `P.ResidueField` has `p`-height at least `n`. -/
theorem heightIdeal_le_prime_iff (hp : p.Prime) {n : ℕ} {P : Ideal R} [P.IsPrime] :
    F.heightIdeal p n ≤ P ↔
      (n : ℕ∞) ≤ (F.map (algebraMap R P.ResidueField)).height p := by
  nth_rw 1 [← P.ker_algebraMap_residueField]
  exact F.heightIdeal_le_ker_iff_le_height hp _

end FormalGroup
